<main>
  <a class="brand" href="/">yago</a>
  <h1>Use the agent API</h1>
  <p>Yago provides a Tavily-compatible HTTP API on this host. Requests use JSON and a bearer API key.</p>

  <h2>Create an API key</h2>
  <p>In Admin, open <a href="/admin/security">Security</a> and create a Search API key. Give it <code>search:read</code> for ordinary search. Add <code>search:raw</code> to request full page content or use Extract, Crawl, and Map. The key secret is shown once when created.</p>

  <h2>Search</h2>
  <p>Send a JSON request to <code>POST /search</code>:</p>
  <pre><code>export YAGO_URL="https://your-yago-host"
export YAGO_API_KEY="your-search-api-key"

curl "$YAGO_URL/search" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $YAGO_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query":"open source Go search engine","max_results":5}'</code></pre>

  <h2>Other endpoints</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>POST /extract</code> — extract content from one or more URLs.</li>
    <li><code>POST /crawl</code> — crawl a bounded set of pages from a URL.</li>
    <li><code>POST /map</code> — discover URLs without returning page content.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These endpoints require <code>search:raw</code>. All four endpoints accept JSON POST requests and return JSON.</p>
  <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/D4rk4/yago/blob/dev/yagonode/doc/compatibility.md#agent-api-targets">full API reference</a> for request fields, limits, response formats, and error behavior.</p>

  <p class="foot"><a href="/">Back to search</a></p>
</main>
</body>
